    "status": "present",
    "value": "Represent a polynomial as a map from a sorted tuple of variable names (the monomial) to an integer coefficient; the empty tuple is the constant. Parse with the classic grammar expr := term (('+'|'-') term)*, term := factor ('*' factor)*, factor := number | name | '(' expr ')'. A factor becomes a one-term polynomial (a known variable becomes a constant), addition merges maps with a sign, and multiplication combines every pair of terms by concatenating and re-sorting their variable tuples. Zero coefficients are removed after each operation. Finally sort terms by (-degree, variables) and format them."
  },
